<%# TRIAL, off by default (only /?glass=1, 2 or 3 renders it; the owner is
    comparing placements). A glass that fills as the reader scrolls through
    the story: empty at the first step, full at the closing beat ("That's
    the whole ritual."). Everything for it is here and in
    story_glass_controller.js; to drop the trial, delete both files, the two
    lines in home/index.html.erb and test/integration/home_story_glass_test.rb.

    locals: variant (1, 2 or 3; home/index validates the param, so nothing
    from the request reaches this partial).
      1  Desktop: 64px, in the gutter beside the face's bottom bar.
         Phones: 28px on the right edge, mid-screen.
      2  Desktop: a 96px gauge in the gutter between the step words and the
         face, held at the middle of the screen. Phones: 40px in the
         bottom-right corner.
      3  Desktop: 80px, standing centred under the pinned face, like the
         glass in front of the screen. Phones: 40px on the right edge, just
         under the nav.
    The drawing is shared/_glass at full, its level lowered by the
    controller (the liquid is translated down, as in the pour). It is a
    gauge, so it stays out of the appear controller's pour. Out of the flow
    everywhere (fixed on phones; sticky with no height on desktop), so it
    moves nothing. aria-hidden, no words, absent without JS. On phones it
    sits in the page's 20px gutter (only the glass's empty margin reaches
    past it), never over text, the nav or a tap target, and it lets taps
    through. Under reduced motion the level does not follow the scroll: it
    steps a third at a time as each step is reached, with no motion. %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <style>
    .hx .story-glass { position: fixed; z-index: 30; right: -5px; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 200ms var(--motion-ease-out); }
    .hx .story-glass.is-shown { opacity: 1; }
    .hx .story-glass svg { display: block; width: 30px; height: 40px; }
    .hx .story-glass svg g > path { transform: translateY(var(--story-glass-drop, 38px)); }
    .hx .story-glass--1 { right: 0; top: 50%; margin-top: -14px; }
    .hx .story-glass--1 svg { width: 21px; height: 28px; }
    .hx .story-glass--2 { bottom: calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px)); }
    .hx .story-glass--3 { top: 92px; }
    @media (min-width: 900px) {
      /* Shares the faces' column and sticky top, from the first step to the
         end of the story. The frame matches the face's box, so the glass can
         be placed against the face. */
      .hx .story-glass { position: sticky; grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2 / 6; align-self: start; height: 0; right: auto; bottom: auto; margin: 0;
                         top: max(112px, calc(50svh - 17.5vw)); opacity: 1; transition: none; }
      .hx .story-glass-frame { position: relative; padding: 10px; }
      .hx .story-glass-frame::before { content: ""; display: block; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; }
      .hx .story-glass-frame::after { content: ""; display: block; height: 40px; }
      .hx .story-glass-frame svg { position: absolute; }
      .hx .story-glass--1 .story-glass-frame svg { bottom: 4px; left: -60px; width: 48px; height: 64px; }
      /* 2: held at the middle of the screen in the 72px gutter. */
      .hx .story-glass--2 { top: calc(50svh - 48px); }
      .hx .story-glass--2 .story-glass-frame { padding: 0; }
      .hx .story-glass--2 .story-glass-frame::before, .hx .story-glass--2 .story-glass-frame::after { display: none; }
      .hx .story-glass--2 .story-glass-frame svg { top: 0; left: -72px; width: 72px; height: 96px; }
      /* 3: centred under the face, 28px below its bottom edge. */
      .hx .story-glass--3 .story-glass-frame svg { top: calc(100% + 28px); left: calc(50% - 30px); width: 60px; height: 80px; }
      /* The next face slides up over it, like a screen passing in front of
         the glass on the table, rather than the glass floating on top. */
      .hx .story:has(> .story-glass--3) > .face { z-index: 31; }
    }
    @media (min-width: 1400px) { .hx .story-glass:not(.story-glass--2) { top: max(112px, calc(50svh - 230px)); } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .hx .story-glass { transition: none; } }
    @media print { .hx .story-glass { display: none; } }
  </style>
<% end %>
<% variant_class = { 1 => "story-glass--1", 2 => "story-glass--2", 3 => "story-glass--3" }.fetch(variant) %>
<div class="story-glass <%= variant_class %>" data-controller="story-glass" hidden aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="story-glass-frame">
    <%= render "shared/glass", level: 1, size: 96, appear: false %>
  </div>
</div>
